name duel-merge-1
timeout 300

# THE ASYMMETRIC DUEL, GEOMETRY 6: THE MERGE — the one place the MiG-29's weapon set is not the
# inferior one, and therefore the mission that has to exist before the campaign may claim the F-16
# dominates. The four BVR geometries all turn on radar reach and Rtr, and on both the MiG is behind by
# construction (2.0x and 1.7x, measured). Inside the merge neither matters: an R-73 is cued off the
# helmet, a GSh-301 round carries 2.7x the energy of an M61A1 round, and the airframe out-turns and
# out-rolls the F-16 (measured corner 420 kt / 24.2 deg/s against 380 / 16.2; roll plant 201 deg/s per
# full deflection against 78.7).
#
# THE SETUP: 8 km apart, head-on, co-altitude, both on `set task bfm` — the close-combat control law
# on both sides, no BVR phase and no long shot. Both start inside every launch zone either side has.
#
# THE MiG NOW ACQUIRES IN THE MERGE. gap 4h's acquisition half is closed this round: the pilot switches
# the N019 to ACM in the fight phase (pilot/FBPilot::BfmSelectRadarMode + FBMig29Pilot::BfmRadarModeOrdinal
# = the broad forward auto-lock volume FBMig29Radar::kAcm*, ±37 deg az from T4 §7.1 read as azimuth, a
# ±30 deg vertical band, Doppler-exempt like CC), so the auto-lock does the designation the earlier RAD
# bar could never make. The narrow RAD/CC/VS/BORE pencils are unchanged and still used elsewhere
# (mig29-r73). The F-16 is in ACM HUD as before.
#
# READING RULE: exit 2 (CRASH), and it is a NEW, DEEPER finding rather than the old departure reproducer
# or the old acquisition draw. Measured this round:
#   FULCRUM (MiG): ACQUIRES — n019 MODE acm at t=0.5, RADAR_LOCK at t=3.8 (3.32 nm, az -0.2, el -7.8),
#     lock_s 14.2. The acquisition half of gap 4h is closed: the MiG locks the F-16 in a turning merge on
#     its own radar, where before (RAD) it never got a contact (lock_s 0).
#   VIPER (F-16): DEPARTS at t=18.0 — result=LOC "sustained high multi-axis body rate". Its own UNCAPPED
#     BFM roll law (BfmRollRateMaxDegS 90, BfmSearchRollCap 1.0 — the F-16 defaults, unchanged this round)
#     goes into a full-deflection roll-reversal PIO at the close-in high-closure reversal (rollCmd flips
#     -1 -> +1 -> -1 from t=14.9). It is CAUSAL to the MiG's new acquisition: with the MiG's ACM disabled
#     the F-16 does not depart and the run is exit 3 again (verified this round). The MiG flies aggressive
#     locked pursuit now, and the F-16's roll law cannot hold the reversal.
# So the merge's blocker MOVED AGAIN: departure half (control law) -> acquisition half (sensor, closed
# this round) -> the F-16's own roll PIO at the reversal. The R-73/GSh-301 WEAPON thesis stays untested:
# the fight ends in the F-16's departure before either side employs a WVR weapon. Per the campaign rule a
# loss to an AI defect is not a result, so this is NOT "the MiG wins the merge" — it is a newly exposed
# F-16 BFM roll-law limit, and the next merge blocker. doc/duels.md D1.

unit viper
  team friendly
  module f16
  spawn 46.90000 6.95000 5000 90.0 380
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set datalink off
  set fcr_mode acm_hud                      # auto-locks the nearest firm track: no thumb needed
  set fcr_range_nm 10
  set rwr on
  set store 3 aim9
  set store 7 aim9
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task bfm
  wp 46.90000 7.20000 5000 380
  objective kill unit fulcrum
  objective survive

unit fulcrum
  team hostile
  module mig29
  spawn 46.90000 7.05500 5000 270.0 380
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set n019_mode rad                         # BVR default; the BFM pilot switches to ACM in the fight
  set n019_range_nm 10
  set n019_emission illum
  set rwr on
  set store 3 r73
  set store 4 r73
  set cmds_mode man                          # the MiG can now defend too (BVP-30-26, this round)
  set cmds_chaff 30
  set cmds_flare 30
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task bfm
  wp 46.90000 6.80000 5000 380
  objective kill unit viper
  objective survive
